Tipperary, yeah. Tipperary. Grains Mokler in South Tipperary. He was the Tipperary, Grains Mochler in South Tipperary. He was the only player killed. He was killed crawling off the pitch down in front of Hill 16. He'd been playing on a famous Dublin footballer called Frank Burke, who managed to get off the field. And one of the stands here is named after him.

63
